==English==

===Etymology===
A variant of {{m|en|dungeon}} remodelled on its [[etymon]], {{der|en|fro|donjon}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɒn.d͡ʒən/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɑn.d͡ʒən/|a=US,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɔn.d͡ʒən/|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[fortified]] [[tower]] and main residence of a [[motte]] or early [[castle]]; a [[keep]].
#* {{RQ:Scott Ivanhoe|volume=II|chapter=VII|page=106|passage=It was a fortress of no great size, consisting of a '''donjon''', or large and high square tower, surrounded by buildings of inferior height, which were encircled by an inner court-yard.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Michael Chabon|title=Gentlemen of the Road|publisher=Sceptre|year_published=2008|page=132
|passage={{...}} the prison fortress called Qomr, a mound of yellowish brick rising up from the left back of the turbid river, in whose '''donjon''' by long tradition the warlord was obliged to lay his head.}}

